{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made","id":902405,"title":"Greatest, weirdest, and other-est gods you've made?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-28T18:17:03-07:00","id":902405,"title":"Greatest, weirdest, and other-est gods you've made?","content":"Hey, with the new edition and a lot of new locations, was wondering what some of the strange or cool gods people have come up with? Restore any old ones from the prior editions (I know I loved Swan Dragon in Second Edition) or filling new holes (Lots of place still empty)<br /> I know I've got an ambitious storm god who loves lions down in the Dreaming Sea, who's small for now (just got some authority over storms, started out supervising jungle cats) who's worshiped on the outskirts of Parsaad. So far from an already isolated satrapy, and he's started amassing more power among his followers. Thinking of naming him Endad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:35:22-07:00","id":902419,"title":"","content":"Mostly as the stories need them. Except most of the popular gods (the important official of Yu-Shan) or the ones in the exigent exalted spread (Plentimon, Burning Feathers I think for one of them etc...) are guaranteed to be in my game, forgot the name of the Mountain God with the cult of the illuminated Boot camp in first edition but definitely bringing him back. I also look at the Gods nowadays with which ones are either most likely to sacrifice themselves to make an exigent, go buy black market exaltation for whatever reason or have a chosen.<br /> <br /> A Lytek exigent and Ryzala exigent could be potentially interesting in any chronicle/story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T22:52:15-07:00","id":902498,"title":"","content":"Shimmering White Eyes (from 1E's <i>Cult of the Illuminated</i>) was sweet. So human and yet so alien at the same time.<br /> And I've always preferred god characters who are literally and/or thematically tied to their purview, rather than gods who just seem like superpowered humans. So seeing White's emotions be explicitly connected to her patron spring, to see it being treated as an aspect/extension of herself, was really cool. She doesn't just work through her spring, she <i>is</i> her spring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:28:10-07:00","id":902508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=902419#post902419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Lytek exigent and Ryzala exigent could be potentially interesting in any chronicle/story.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I like Lytek, I imagine both him and Ryzala's reason for exigents would be suspect if not illegal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T02:22:31-07:00","id":902583,"title":"","content":"Oh definitely, even if from what I had in mind, Lytek with nobody to trust about the Great curse, would make an exigent incognito to have him investigate the matter, since Lytek can't do it and his defining principle is that all exalted achieves greatness, so making an exigent to help achieve and fix his work...seems kind of something that he would do.<br /> <br /> Ryzala in my mind, would use her exigent to be against the Sidereals to say the least, well to be more exact the bronze faction while she doesn't embrace the gold faction, could definitely see her making an exigent just for this purpose, illegally of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:23:19-07:00","id":902638,"title":"","content":"We've got an Exigent of Ryzala in our Sidereals game. She's neat, her powers are paper based and she utilises prayer strips but in a different way to our characters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:51:54-07:00","id":902748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=902638#post902638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've got an Exigent of Ryzala in our Sidereals game. She's neat, her powers are paper based and she utilises prayer strips but in a different way to our characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on this Gamilah (the Exigent in question) uses her prayer strips to invoke the aid of external powers that serve or aid Heaven. For her its not about devotion or enlightenment so much as knowing how to ask for things and using paper as a medium.<br /> <br /> For example: if she wants to avoid freezing to death in the North she writes a prayer to Hesiesh and sticks it to herself to stay warm. To expand on this ability she experiments and devises other applications for a strip of paper invested with the warmth of the Fire Dragon. It seems harmless enough, but what if instead of distributing that heat over a long period of time she can use multiple prayer strips to produce a different outcome or damage one to release this heat much faster? Bureaucracy is as much about knowing when to bend the rules as well as knowing when to use them like a cudgel.<br /> <br /> Essentially she has a different take on the adaptable and advanced planning aspects of Sidereals while dispensing with ideas of destiny and enlightenment which Ryzala fears and distrusts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:24:46-07:00","id":902793,"title":"","content":"The heaviest god I've ever come up with, and the one that uses the largest fonts:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:36px\">MO-FUM-BO THE RICE GOD!</span><br /> <br /> In my games, Mo-fum-bo is the god is rice in the South. On his left is a massive pile of bowls of cooked white rice. On his right is a massive pile of empty bowls. He eats continuously, shoveling in rice with chopsticks, bowl after bowl. He never drops a single grain. Around his throne are a horde of spirits who act as cooks and bowl-washers, and one interpreter, who explains to his petitioners the meanings of his incomprehensible, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q8qnGcLKTdI\" target=\"_blank\">Strong-Mad</a>-like grumbletalk.<br /> <br /> He's basically my favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":2240,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","user":"Colin_Fredericks","date":". 11-09-2020, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:20:58-07:00","id":902829,"title":"","content":"One homebrew god I used extensively in one campaign and as a major figure in another. The god in question was Aurenna. In addition to being the goddess of various sorts of jungle spiders she was a member of the Bureau of Battles and is a subordinate to Sunipa the god of Eastern Warfare. In her capacity as a war goddess she represented asymmetrical warfare. She focused on things like ambushes, poisoning your enemies food and water, assassination, and essentially any sort of dishonorable or unfair technique.<br /> <br /> In much of the East, where the large forests and jungles make the massing of large standing armies impossible, Aurenna is the defacto goddess of war and is often worshiped as such by the tribes who live in those areas. She is engaged in a millennium long plot to overthrow and replace Sunpia as the Eastern goddess of warfare, not solely for personal power (though there is that), but because she is convinced Sunpia assisted in the murder of her lover, Darunla the previous goddess of Eastern warfare.<br /> <br /> She made a useful (if somewhat creepy and heartless) ally in a Solar game I was running, and a useful foil in a Bronze Faction game I later ran.<br /> <br /> One of my players expressed interest in playing an Exigent of hers when 3rd edition came out, so I've been considering how to put a Charmset together.<br /> <br /> Another fun god I used was Joe, a Bloody Hand who was assigned to watch and record the murders of a Night Caste assassin PC. Joe would often help the PC, but he could also be kind of annoying. &quot;Hey, hey, hey. Why don't you kill him with... uhhh... how about that rock there? No? Maybe that paperweight then? Just club him on the head. I'll bet it'll kill him.&quot;<br /> <br /> *EDIT* I ran Joe kind of like Morte from Planescape Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-29-2016, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:46:01-07:00","id":903023,"title":"","content":"Two whom I mentioned on another thread are Brings Joy in the Morning, and Painful Footstep.<br /> <br /> Brings Joy was the local crop god of coffee on an island ruled by a shark god who had the locals paint their canoes with blood and coffee to drive away dolphin spirits. After the party ousted the shark god, Brings Joy in the Morning got the locals to brew and drink coffee and to trade it overseas. He was working to establish himself as the local cultural god, with a coffeehouse/temple attended by barista/priestesses in green liturgical aprons.<br /> <br /> Painful Footstep was the god of a minor species of scorpion wiped out by the Great Contagion, and he now works for the Gold Star Signatories of the Sun's Favor. He(or possibly she, it's hard to tell with giant scorpions) is hard-working, dedicated and believes in moving up through the system by being the best qualified. It is also a backstabbing suck-up who, when one of the PC's got himself appointed manager of the Signatories, would be there every morning with the boss' double latte' extra sugar, a box of celestial doughnuts, and a list of other employees who need to be fired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11828-ikari-gendo","name":"Ikari Gendo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T15:58:46-07:00","id":903067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ikari Gendo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=903023#post903023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brings Joy was the local crop god of coffee on an island ruled by a shark god who had the locals paint their canoes with blood and coffee to drive away dolphin spirits. After the party ousted the shark god, Brings Joy in the Morning got the locals to brew and drink coffee and to trade it overseas. He was working to establish himself as the local cultural god, with a coffeehouse/temple attended by barista/priestesses in green liturgical aprons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've paid tribute to this god I believe. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T16:29:47-07:00","id":903087,"title":"","content":"I used the God of Tapeworms although he/she shouldn't count because it is on the cover of two books. I liked the god of theater (too lazy to look up the name right now) who became friends with the PCs to make sure plays about their adventures are seen by all. He got into a fight once and used stage fighting techniques that looked fake but did real damage.<br /> <br /> I also have the God of Gold in my current game who has been in an argument with the salt gods and trade gods about currency for about 200 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:20:24-07:00","id":903633,"title":"","content":"Somewhat on topic I had an idea that every major office in yu-shan came with an emergency exigency as part of the bonus/duty of the office. Basically the four directional gods of war, the beauru heads, and a few other powerful deities have one guaranteed authorized exigency that they may use in case of personal emergency but that they absolutely must use in case of true emergency. This protocol was enacted after the balorian crusade when it was determined there needed to be a quick way to empower potent mortals to aid in times of crisis. So far in my canon none of these exigencies have been used but the potential is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:30:54-07:00","id":903677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=903633#post903633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhat on topic I had an idea that every major office in yu-shan came with an emergency exigency as part of the bonus/duty of the office. Basically the four directional gods of war, the beauru heads, and a few other powerful deities have one guaranteed authorized exigency that they may use in case of personal emergency but that they absolutely must use in case of true emergency. This protocol was enacted after the balorian crusade when it was determined there needed to be a quick way to empower potent mortals to aid in times of crisis. So far in my canon none of these exigencies have been used but the potential is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Break in case of doom sort of thing?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:31:43-07:00","id":903678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MuscaDomestica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=903087#post903087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also have the God of Gold in my current game who has been in an argument with the salt gods and trade gods about currency for about 200 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the God of Jade? I imagine earth elementals have a say too. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:58:03-07:00","id":903694,"title":"","content":"Three I made for other threads:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808953-purviews-what-are-you-the-god-of\">Purviews: What are you the god of:</a><br /> <br /> The Great and Gluttonous Jal - God of Over-Eating - Once serving under Venus, he was moved to the Division of Endings due to one too many deaths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your mother is a *beep beep beep*ing*beep*<a href=\"http://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=lorem+ipsum\" target=\"_blank\">lorem ipsum</a>*beep beep beep*admiumvenium*beep beep beep beep*turolagulio*beep beep beep beep beep beep beep beep* hippopotamus*beep beep beep beep beep beep* Republican *beep beep beep* <a href=\"http://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=Daniel+Radcliffe\" target=\"_blank\">Daniel Radcliffe</a> *beep beep beep beep* with a bucket of *beep beep beep beep* in a castle far away where no one can hear you *beep beep beep beep beep beep* soup *beep beep beep* with a bucket of *beep beep* Mickey Mouse *beep beep* with a stick of dinomite *beeeeeepppp* magical *beep beep beep beep* ALAKAZAMER -God of Swears - Bureau of Humanity, but only has an official post due to his loud mouth being so annoying that he was able to arrange for a job.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/230177-forbidden-gods\">Forbidden gods</a>:<br /> <br /> <b>Name a god: </b>Vhe Vungry Vaw (The Hungry Maw)<br /> <b>Describe your god: </b>Basically an oversized head on a tiny body with a giant oversized mouth, with oversized teeth. When he is not smiling inanly like a mad man, he devours everything in sight, particularly paperwork. Also mispronounces every word with the first letter replaced with the letter V.<br /> <b>Describe your god's origins: </b>He started out as a loose tooth in a behemoth that Autochthon spun a body out of the hungry cries of babies and held it all in place with needles made from the bones of all the first devouring beasts.<br /> <b>Tell why your god is forbidden: </b>As the god of things with endless hunger, he was hungry and he ate a lot of paper work in the move to Yu Shan, damn important paperwork! Also his speech impediment got annoying after a while.<br /> <b>Describe your god's location: </b>Tied down with chains of jade and orichalcum in a deep pit under the Imperial City which waste is dumped down every now and again.<br /> <b>Describe your god's current goals: </b>Get out of the pit and eat better and more common varied food then refuse, preferably paper work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T12:06:57-07:00","id":903699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ikari Gendo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=903023#post903023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was working to establish himself as the local cultural god, with a coffeehouse/temple attended by barista/priestesses in green liturgical aprons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was so close to liking this. <i>So close</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:15:10-07:00","id":904346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=903694#post903694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/230177-forbidden-gods\">Forbidden gods</a>:<br /> <br /> <b>Name a god: </b>Vhe Vungry Vaw (The Hungry Maw)<br /> <b>Describe your god: </b>Basically an oversized head on a tiny body with a giant oversized mouth, with oversized teeth. When he is not smiling inanly like a mad man, he devours everything in sight, particularly paperwork. Also mispronounces every word with the first letter replaced with the letter V.<br /> <b>Describe your god's origins: </b>He started out as a loose tooth in a behemoth that Autochthon spun a body out of the hungry cries of babies and held it all in place with needles made from the bones of all the first devouring beasts.<br /> <b>Tell why your god is forbidden: </b>As the god of things with endless hunger, he was hungry and he ate a lot of paper work in the move to Yu Shan, damn important paperwork! Also his speech impediment got annoying after a while.<br /> <b>Describe your god's location: </b>Tied down with chains of jade and orichalcum in a deep pit under the Imperial City which waste is dumped down every now and again.<br /> <b>Describe your god's current goals: </b>Get out of the pit and eat better and more common varied food then refuse, preferably paper work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet, love the idea of Forbidden Gods. I hope we get some more named ones (most I remember were generic except the wonderful cannibalism god in the East).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:48:58-07:00","id":904510,"title":"","content":"Alright, latest one from myself:<br /> Ten Faced Yen, a god who looks a little less than human and is the father-god of the Yennin. Being of the Yennin and Volviat, he has ten aspects: King,Warrior, Poet,Scholar, Judge, Father, Mercnaht, Priest,Craftsmen, and a hidden tenth nature only he knows. Ten Faced Yen seeks to expand the power of Volviat (of course) and claims credit for teaching the method of many fathers. He's a masters of none god, but a dabbler in all, and is always intreasted in learning any bit of knowledge he can, as well as acquiring new lovers to father more children that Volviat would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:54:25-07:00","id":904512,"title":"","content":"I made up Much-Curse Yao, the God of Stubbing Your Little Toe in the Middle of the Night. He has a surprisingly large Cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T03:40:33-07:00","id":904829,"title":"","content":"They don't necessarily count as 'cool' by any count, but for a possible upcoming game I created an uptight and somewhat unhinged minor Road God whose domain winds through several small villages in the East. He's come to value keeping his road in pristine condition more than letting people use it for its intended purpose, to the point where he nearly throws a tantrum every time someone walks on it in a way he dislikes, and is currently having a petty feud with the little god of a sacred old cherry tree in one of the villages, whose tree constantly sheds petals onto his road and who refuses to apologize for this. Their fight and the inconveniences it is causing the local mortals is intended to serve as a simple and humorous little sidequest between the actual challenges the pcs face and/or just be exists to add a bit of lighthearted flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:04:46-07:00","id":905161,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I ran a game where the party played gods we had some good ones in that. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One played the standard bearer of the Unconquered Sun a winged Goddess that since the Time of Glory would appear at battles important to the Guarding Star. She would grant his favor by carrying his standard into the battle. The standard would then bless the force whose camp she held it aloft in for as long as she kept it raised. She favored the Solar Exalted and became sullen when they grew corrupt she neither opposed nor aided the Usurpation however she detested the act of imprisoning their power. She followed the Unconquered Sun's lead in turning her face from creation until the Fey invasion where she flew about blessing whatever resistance stood bravest against the endless horde. In the modern time she watches the Solar Exalted carefully judging if they have returned heros or threats determined to bless the worthy and oppose the corrupt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll post a couple more when I have time</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I used to be Median but life has made me Mean.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1753-avrjoe","name":"Avrjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1753_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:51:14-07:00","id":905315,"title":"","content":"From the same campaign as Brings Joy in the Morning, the party had to find a more powerful deity to protect the island. They wound up in Yu-Shan, interviewing unemployed gods and goddesses, and finally settled on Lyesha, former Goddess of Harbors and International Trade in sunken Luthe. Picture your 80 year old bitter spinster aunt living in a big house full of antique bric-a-brac, but rather than cats, she has carp in her water filled sanctum. The carp act like cats, bumping your ankles, getting in your face, nuzzling your face, and just being annoying. The whole place smells like carp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11828-ikari-gendo","name":"Ikari Gendo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T19:37:49-07:00","id":905336,"title":"","content":"I've run a couple of campaigns where characters stumble across the little town of Amoree, benevolently ruled by Dayless Dawn, aspect-god of the Unconquered Sun. Dayless comes across a little weird - he doesn't have four arms, for characters who know about that sort of thing, and he's kind of pale and thin for a guy who claims to be a manifestation of the Sun. Still, he and his heavily-robed priest-children rule the town peacefully and well from the old stone temple on the top of the hill, so what's the harm?<br /> <br /> A little digging reveals that Amoree was founded after the Contagion, when a wandering band of survivors stumbled onto the temple and found the statue of the Sun inside. No, not a big humanoid Sol like in the corebook - a statue of the <i>Sun</i>. You know, a big crystal orb? Glows somewhere deep inside? It's up there in the temple, the one surrounded by all those priests with what looks suspiciously like radiation burns - the one that, if someone actually competent at Old Realm gets a look at it, clearly says <i>Armory </i>just inside the front door.<br /> <br /> ... he's a soulbreaker orb - or, well, the god of soulbreaker orb, who through some combination of focused devotion and lots of time is evolving into something more. Trouble is, whatever else he becomes, he's <i>still the god of a fantasy nuke</i>, and sooner or later that sucker's going to go boom.<br /> <br /> This usually leads to some fun discussions. In my current game, Dayless Dawn has begrudgingly worked with &quot;My beloved Chosen&quot; (i.e., the party) to fight off a fae army; as a result, he's now the focus of a growing cult in the area. That's troubling for the party; what's troubling for <i>him</i>, sneaky jerk that he is, is that the more people worship him as a font of virtue, the more he feels the urge to be exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:27:05-07:00","id":905955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=903678#post903678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the God of Jade? I imagine earth elementals have a say too. </div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost positive that the Magical Materials were explicitly stated as having no god overseeing their roles in Creation, putting them in the same category of &quot;godless&quot; things as sorcery, martial arts, and Essence itself.<br /> <br /> Of course, with Exalted's sprawling lore (<i>X</i> books in three editions, plus errata, plus the Ink Monkeys stuff online), I'll be damned if I can remember exactly where I read that. I'll see if I can track it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:54:36-07:00","id":906024,"title":"","content":"<b>Abacusith</b>, The God of Accounting.<br /> <br /> He doesn't get invited to parties anymore; the clicking got annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T21:54:06-07:00","id":906204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=905955#post905955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm almost positive that the Magical Materials were explicitly stated as having no god overseeing their roles in Creation, putting them in the same category of &quot;godless&quot; things as sorcery, martial arts, and Essence itself.<br /> <br /> Of course, with Exalted's sprawling lore (<i>X</i> books in three editions, plus errata, plus the Ink Monkeys stuff online), I'll be damned if I can remember exactly where I read that. I'll see if I can track it down.</div> </div> </div> </div> Forgot jade money was the same as jade the MM. Paper might be a better example then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T22:55:04-07:00","id":906226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=905955#post905955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm almost positive that the Magical Materials were explicitly stated as having no god overseeing their roles in Creation, putting them in the same category of &quot;godless&quot; things as sorcery, martial arts, and Essence itself.<br /> <br /> Of course, with Exalted's sprawling lore (<i>X</i> books in three editions, plus errata, plus the Ink Monkeys stuff online), I'll be damned if I can remember exactly where I read that. I'll see if I can track it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T23:03:05-07:00","id":906231,"title":"","content":"The gods of the Five Magic Materials are addressed specifically on page 62 of Yu-Shan. There are five goddesses of Jade according to the sidebar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:40:04-07:00","id":906639,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Pffffbbt, </b></u><u><b>Daimyo of the Five Passing Winds, Shepherd of Odiferous Airs, Overseer of Nightentide Ovens, Captain of the Silent Fume</b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">He's the God of Farts, yo. And he actually became important because he was being shunted out of heaven despite his wide purview of the gaseous release of all living things. We helped him, and he backed us up when we needed him through his ability to appear wherever there was a lingering fart in the air. Getting his attention required flatulance of... just epic proportions. I needed to have the Zenith roll Stamina Resistance to be able to safely take the amount of beans he was eating.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T22:42:25-07:00","id":907461,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#626566\"><span style=\"font-family:Brutal Type\"><b>Here's a guy I wrote for a prompt on tumblr, here's the full writeup of the manse: </b><a href=\"http://magicturtle.tumblr.com/post/116313126147/exalted-challenge-entry-diadem-heart\" target=\"_blank\">http://magicturtle.tumblr.com/post/1...y-diadem-heart</a><br /> <br /> <b>Cygmo-Channo</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#626566\"><span style=\"font-family:Brutal Type\">The god of Diadem Heart, Cygmo-Channo is cold, cruel and aloof, but more so than any of those he is arrogant. Thus, any family member (or current target of Pyre\u2019s indoctrination) can ask him for information regarding spirits, ancient artifacts or (immaculate approved) realm history, and as long as he is properly praised, he is happy to answer. Cygmo-Channo\u2019s relationship with Inconspicuous Pyre is professional, he knows that as long as the Bronze faction is in control, he has nothing to gain by going against them, furthermore, he derives a cruel joy from watching his manse affect the brains of others, dragonblooded especially. Cygmo-Channo appears as a large, perfectly round, glowing sphere that has been shoved into some fancy clothes, sleeves and pant legs dangle as it floats back and forth. His voice is deep, but has an ethereal quality. His entire sphere-body glows when he speaks.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6228-canis-vulgaris","name":"Canis Vulgaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6228_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T23:39:13-07:00","id":907483,"title":"","content":"A game I ran for awhile featured <b>Bari Hee, Goddess of Last Hopes and Desperate Pleas</b>. She was a mid level goddess, prayed to by the most desperate, by those who had tried every recourse and failed to have anything be fixed. She was a loving woman who had 'an innumerable number of arms, with which to hold the poor souls who called on her'. She did what she could for anyone who needed her, though her powers were limited, and was also known as <b>Bari Hee, the Crying Goddess</b>, for her compassion was such that not once in her lifetime had she ever stopped crying, the inability to save everyone driving her to cry for their losses, and her own weakness. It was such that even in the face of Sol himself she could not cease her tears,and even he was said to have been moved by this weak god's compassion, for the slightest of moments, a golden tear running down his face, and touching to her head - it is said that this is why the dark skinned goddess normally clad in mourning black does now have shining golden hair.<br /> <br /> I hope to one day find a way to create an Exigent from her, because I enjoyed creating her, and my players practically fell in love with her - it derailed the campaign for like 10 sessions, as everyone tried to scramble to make her less sad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 06-11-2016, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T05:32:32-07:00","id":907574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=904346#post904346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sweet, love the idea of Forbidden Gods. I hope we get some more named ones (most I remember were generic except the wonderful cannibalism god in the East).</div> </div> </div> </div>This goddess almost always leaves a lasting impression:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/2285.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://l-stat.livejournal.net/img/sign.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/2285.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Chitsu, Goddess of Vaginal Devouring (Forbidden God) </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/2285.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/2285.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In the times before the Primordial War, the goddess Chitsu was associated with aspects of both motherly love and regression, but the primary role in which she served Creation was that as Goddess of Vaginal Devouring. Before the Unconquered Sun claimed Yu-Shan for himself and his peers and granted&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T06:06:35-07:00","id":907583,"title":"","content":"I recall someone at one point cooking up a god of nails, who had a rather erotic fascination with hammers, particular artifact diremauls and whatnot.<br /> <br /> I once cooked up a rather bland river goddess - but her gimmick was that she had been aiding a local river pirate lord, who was her lover. She was really pissed the players offed the pirate lord, and demanded that they find her a suitably handsome and charming replacement lover, otherwise there'd be hell to pay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T16:11:06-07:00","id":910388,"title":"","content":"In our game, our dawn caste is a drunken destruction hobo. Someone botched an astrology roll, and now &quot;The God of Poor Choices Made While Drunk&quot; is hounding the dawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11315-remulader","name":"Remulader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11315_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T07:23:01-07:00","id":1413370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=902508#post902508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like Lytek, I imagine both him and Ryzala's reason for exigents would be suspect if not illegal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, the canonicity of Lytek's purview in 3e is kind of debatable in the first place.<br /> <br /> Me i changed him into a god of memories and remembrance, what gets him out of that weird place of having a weirdly specific/niche domain that still must also be imensely powerful - while keeping his story hooks and portrayal mostly intact. With Parad things were much easier, as &quot;Inherited Might&quot; can be a reasonably broad concept that is far from limited to the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=907583#post907583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall someone at one point cooking up a god of nails, who had a rather erotic fascination with hammers, particular artifact diremauls and whatnot.<br /> <br /> I once cooked up a rather bland river goddess - but her gimmick was that she had been aiding a local river pirate lord, who was her lover. She was really pissed the players offed the pirate lord, and demanded that they find her a suitably handsome and charming replacement lover, otherwise there'd be hell to pay.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think of a game i once set, where a lake goddess found out about a river god with a taste for the attention of local village maidens - and then went and seduced the river god (that was basically a lecherous Okuto, with a claw strider/mandarin duck alternate form), getting his attention and to make part of her work for her and the thanks/worship of the villagers, that weren't pressed by the river god for female company anymore.<br /> <br /> (What didn't stop either deity from getting the occasional petitioner/fling on the side, but that's another story - specially when the goddess last conquest/hostage turned out into more than she bargained for) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also made funny minor elementals like the cabbage-born, that could really, really blur the lines between human and supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-21-2020, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T03:02:23-07:00","id":1413517,"title":"","content":"I had a Mary Poppins knock-off God of Childcare. Nameless because she never appeared in the game. Long ago, Venus cheated in the Games of Divinity and as punishment Sol stabbed her with his spear. Every inch of the Maiden's body was a constellation representing a God under her purview, and the attack blasted their star out of the sky, killing the God. This Starmetal was forged into the core of a Black Jade Daiumbrella with a head on the handle who spoke in the slain God's voice and compelled the bearer to seek out children to tend to.<br /> <br /> There was also Daucus Carota, the God of Carrots. He was a recurring character with an ultimate plan to overthrow the God of Vegetables. He'd show up periodically and switch the player's rations for carrots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T08:56:58-07:00","id":1413787,"title":"","content":"Jishu Xing, God of Technicalities and Nice and Accurate Wording<br /> <br /> Rumors say that in the first age, a Sidereal once used End Debate to permanently make Jishu incorruptible ... And he showed up to work the next day with a smile and no visible effects. The truth of this is unknown, but even Elder Sidereals don't discount it.<br /> <br /> Jishu Xing is a scrupulously honest and proper God, as well as one of the biggest scoundrels in Heaven. He has been audited many times, only to be exonerated in each case. At the mention of his involvement, Celestial Lions throw up their hands in despair. He has a very properly sized (if only just) Celestial Manse, and an appropriate Salary (on the very high end for his rank). He is a God of Abstract Matters, and he consults for the Forbidding Manse of Ivy, at the request of the Maiden of Secrets. He was very helpful to the Maidens in helping devise the nature of their rebellion against the Primordials.<br /> <br /> Jishu will countersign any Astrology Petition a Sidereal asks him to, provided they affirm and swear that the astrology is permissable under the Laws of Heaven. Every prayer, from mortals, exalts, or other gods is duly written up and reported as a bribery attempt ... and filed by his archivist, a lesser god of madness. His archive contains thousands of years of records, sorted in no way even the God of Filing can comprehend.<br /> <br /> However, Jishu is ultimately and entirely properly concerned with his (technical) righteousness. He will reveal the exact nature of his association with any God or Exalt to a Censor if asked, which has led to multiple convictions, and prevents most Censors from holding a grudge. He has a Sealed Warrant from the Maiden of Secrets which authorizes him to use the Gold Canal (apparently) whenever he wishes.<br /> <br /> Foolish gods and exalts conspire with him. Wise ones can seek out his counsel. He is owed favors by a wide variety of gods. He has always been fond of members of the Eclipse Caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T09:43:56-07:00","id":1413793,"title":"","content":"EDITION WARNING: This deity doesn't work with the way 3E rules work. I still liked her enough to go find her write-up, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Jai-Li, Goddess of the Celestial Practice of the Resplendent Bulb of Understanding<br /> <br /> Jai-Li is a six-armed woman, otherwise appearing as a normal, if nine foot tall, woman. Her skin is the bronzed flesh of a lean, toned warrior, and her hair would kiss the ground were she to take it out of the elaborately braided array she wears it in. Piercing green eyes can flash with anger, but her usual mein is a perfectly inscrutable facade.<br /> <br /> Jai-Li is the goddess of the Celestial Martial Arts ... well, at least the Celestial Exalted practice of the Celestial Martial Arts. And therein lies the rub, and the reason she supports the Cult of the Illuminated. What was once a minor loophole in her purview, has become a major chink in her armor. Other than the Sidereal Exalted, and the (very) occasional Lunar, the vast majority of those practicing Celestial Martial Artists are the Immaculates. Due to her subordinate's close ties with the Bronze Faction (he was apparently involved in helping to disseminate and teach the Immaculate Styles), she has seen her pay and office whittled away, bit by bit as he claimed authority over the Immaculate Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> Jai-Li will tutor any Celestial Exalt in a martial art. This is considered part of the Mandate of the Exalted since the high first age, and cannot result in censure. For Sidereal Exalted without dots in Sifu, Jai-Li is probably their teacher. However, Jai-Li will only teach the Exalt the 'proper' style for them, determined by a criteria understood only by herself. This may include styles thought long lost to creation (at least one young Exalt has recently been learning something called Thousand Wounds Gear Style, which is entirely unknown in the heavenly archives).<br /> <br /> As part of her support for the Garden of Heaven camp of the Cult, Jai-Li has managed to get a ban on teaching any Celestial Martial Arts to the Dragonblooded at the Garden. She is aware and unhappy about Venerable Silk's training at the Hidden Tabernacle, but has been able to be placated thus far. Jai-Li likes to think she is safe from Censors, due to her remit to teach the Exalted, but her donations and assistance to the Cult have gone past what is proper, and should it become necessary, Patient Viper is prepared to blackmail her with the release of this information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T13:07:31-07:00","id":1413821,"title":"","content":"Tan Mo Dei, Daimyo of the Exalted Practice of Shaping Sorcery<br /> <br /> Tan Mo Dei is a relative newcomer, being created for the office he holds after the Primordial War, when Brigid discovered that there was no God for Sorcery. Given the usefulness of Sorcery to the Exalted, his rise in power was astronomical. Somewhat reduced in station after the Usurpation, he is is still a powerful Celestial God, whose favor is often sought by those who seek sorcerous power.<br /> <br /> Tan Mo Dei appears most often as a spinning set of jewel rings, uncountable in number, all revolving around a central axis, his booming voice echoing from that center. The outermost rings are of emerald, shading through sapphire and into adamant as one looks closer to the center, all covered in almost invisibly fine engraving in Old Realm.<br /> <br /> Tan Mo Dei, in either his fully divine form or else as an aged but hale man, with a great beard of the color of his rings, and a staff written with his engraved runes, does his best to appear impartial in any political matter. He offers knowledge, but what someone chooses to do with it is their decision. As such, he often remains aloof from any Heavenly politics. This is because secretly, Tan Mo Dei is afraid of being revealed to be somewhat powerless. The gods did not create Sorcery, and though he is as conversant with the rules and spells of it as the combination of the most experienced sorcerors, he cannot actually cast sorcery beyond the Terrestrial Circle. (His divine authority does allow him to use the effects of Sapphire and Adamant Countermagic, however this is a divine power and not actual sorcery).<br /> <br /> Tan Mo Dei is covertly supporting the Cult of the Illuminated in an effort to regain some of his standing in Heaven. Initially unsure about the return of the Solar Exalted, the fallout of the sorcerous battles between Sidereal backed Realm Legions and the Bull of the North's Circle had an extremely salubrious effect on his popularity in Heaven. Although Initiation, even in the Silurian model is up to the individual Sorceror, Tan Mo Dei is helping the Garden of Heaven train Solars to reach the Circle of Adamant, but only those who visit the Ten Thousand Tea Gardens of Chien. Tan Mo Dei will not leave Heaven. (Rumors that this is due to a falling out with Raksi are often bandied about, but there is no proof). This training is hindered by two factors. <br /> <br /> Firstly, Tan Mo Dei, though appreciative of the Silurian notation, and the Salinian Working, has a pedant's appreciation for the works of Devon, and tends to use abstruse technical terms while speaking of sorcery (the better to impress others with his power and knowledge). For sorcerors who have self-initiated or begun in a different tradition (as many Twilight Caste do, either before or while at the Garden) this makes for an additional barrier to learning. <br /> <br /> Secondly, Tan Mo Dei does not have access to the archives of Solar Circle Spells. While within the purview of his office, the Bronze Faction long ago suborned the archivist in charge of the Solar Circle, using him to help identify and forecast the powers of the Solars for the Usurpation. After the loss of the Tepet Legions, this friendship has been reinforced with bribes and status. Seeking to remain on good terms with all of Heaven, and not yet ready to openly provoke the Bronze, Tan Mo Dei is stepping carefully. Should he have a student achieve the final Initiation, their first spells will likely be evolutions of lower circle spells, such as Adamant Countermagic, Adamant Banishing, or Demon of the Third Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-15-2020, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T16:27:25-07:00","id":1413868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=1413793#post1413793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDITION WARNING: This deity doesn't work with the way 3E rules work. I still liked her enough to go find her write-up, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s very minor what actually changes.<br /> <br /> While there\u2019s no longer a distinct category of Martial Arts called 'Celestial Martial Arts' there is still a Celestial/Mastery level of practicing Martial Arts that Dragon-Blooded can\u2019t normally reach and it would be on brand for a department in Yu-Shan to call that something like The Resplendent Bulb of Understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T19:50:01-07:00","id":1414499,"title":"","content":"So... do martial arts have gods in 3E or not? I'm a bit confused","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T05:05:42-07:00","id":1414544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=1414499#post1414499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... do martial arts have gods in 3E or not? I'm a bit confused</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that in 1-2E, Martial Arts were divided into three tiers. Terrestrial, Celestial, and Sidereal. It was difficult and rare to practice the ones above your pay-grade, as it were. But everyone practiced Snake Style as a Celestial Martial Art. Same rules and everything.. But a regular DB couldn't do it without years of training. Immaculates all could, because that's what the Cloister was for, and all the Immaculate Styles were Celestial Martial Arts, roughly balanced with Solar Charms for power, usable in all armor, and with unique benefits for the Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> In 3E, this sort of difference between martial arts expertise is represented with the Terrestrial and Mastery keywords. So while the Immaculates are still uniquely better with martial arts than other DB, there's less of a fundamental division between Tiger and Water Dragon as Celestial and Jade Mountain and Five Dragon as the somewhat worse Terrestrial styles. (It's significantly more complicated than that. Some TMA had great charms, some CMA were not as well designed. But that was the underlying metaphysical principle of MA in previous editions, that it was gated somewhat similarly to sorcery in theme)<br /> <br /> TL;DR MA probably still has gods in 3E, but a fair bit of this character's specific grievances and motivations are based on a world in which martial arts is divided into formal levels, similar to sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-19-2020, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T07:55:06-07:00","id":1414564,"title":"","content":"Ah, so there can still be a god for each individual martlal art? I was wondering about that because I'm making an occult supernal Eclipse who is also a void point swordsman, and I was thinking of creating a 'patron god' of my style through the occult power that lets you build a spirit familiar from scratch. Now I'm wondering if that would be a legal move or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T09:04:30-07:00","id":1414570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=1414564#post1414564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so there can still be a god for each individual martlal art? I was wondering about that because I'm making an occult supernal Eclipse who is also a void point swordsman, and I was thinking of creating a 'patron god' of my style through the occult power that lets you build a spirit familiar from scratch. Now I'm wondering if that would be a legal move or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So a thing with &quot;gods of a thing&quot; is that the positions are decided by Heaven. Making a spirit of your style should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T16:13:50-07:00","id":1419256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902405-greatest-weirdest-and-other-est-gods-you-ve-made?p=1414564#post1414564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so there can still be a god for each individual martlal art? I was wondering about that because I'm making an occult supernal Eclipse who is also a void point swordsman, and I was thinking of creating a 'patron god' of my style through the occult power that lets you build a spirit familiar from scratch. Now I'm wondering if that would be a legal move or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Definitely possible - the main question i'd say is if there's a good of a style or if the god of swords might attempt to do double or triple duty for the sake of expanding its base of worship, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T11:05:04-07:00","id":1419399,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is the place for it and I'm usually iffy on self promotion, but there is a sort of God in my game that's fairly unique I think, though it also involves a Demon and an Elemental<br /> <br /> In my Shogunate Dragonblooded game, Darunla had three children; one with a God, one with an Elemental, and one with a Demon of Malfean Stock. The three children born thus had no human blood in them, and were instead 'Godlings', each extremely powerful from their mixed blood. The Three, all male, were well known as troublemakers and vagabonds who would wander Creation causing issues and righting wrongs, each uniquely powerful and strong. During the course of the game, the three brothers became enamored with a Godblooded who ascended to Lesser Elemental Dragon via absorbing some of the Essence of a Greater Elemental Dragon, who took the form of a Kirin. The three brothers chased the Kirin around Creation, and eventually they gave her three daughters. The second generation of Godlings, called the Wolfen, are a strange, massive mix of God, Elemental, and Demon, each possessing what amounts to a third of the concept of a thunderstorm.<br /> <br /> Yoko is the oldest, and is the incarnation of Stormclouds and the sound of Thunder, with grey hair<br /> Tora is the middle, and the incarnation of Stormwinds, with green hair<br /> Ina is the youngest, and the incarnation of Lightning Bolts with yellow hair.<br /> <br /> However, the Wolfen have powers that their parents most assuredly don't. They have the ability to combine into singular beings, completely unique, each with their own thoughts, emotions, and powers. While they're combined, the Wolfen themselves cease to exist, which can give them some anxiety about it. In addition to this, each of the beings is fully one type; a God, a Demon, and an Elemental, and each has a position within the structure of each of those types of being's Hierarchy, despite the fact that they only exist in short periods.<br /> <br /> When Yoko and Tora combine, they make Fulgora, the Goddess of Summer Storms.<br /> When Tora and Ina combine, they make Raijin, a Second Circle Demon of Ligier given the title of Demon Lightning<br /> When Yoko and Ina combine, they make Los Lobos, the Lord of the Court of Wild Disasters, who sits in the Empty Chair at the head of their meetings.<br /> <br /> It's somewhat unclear to the players how they manage to attend to their duties while only being in existence for a few hours every now and then, but it's also difficult to question them because the Wolves don't know and they've been too busy to interrogate the actual beings if they care to.<br /> <br /> In this case, the oddness to me doesn't come from what they're the God of, but rather how their existence is very distinct.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}